Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-123: the CSV table checked against Excel's own
 help -- the silent wrong results fixed, the fill keys added (0.123.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20261001: "你看一下網路上 手冊還有哪些操作 或是細部操作 或是目前操作後的結果跟網路上結果不一樣".
Compared with support.microsoft.com (Keyboard shortcuts in Excel, Enter data manually, Edit cell
contents, Find or replace, Move or copy cells). Fixed (each wrote something other than meant):
- one cell pasted on a selected column changed only its first cell -> fills it (lib/csvtable.js
  pasteChanges: a block that fits a whole number of times repeats; a cut block moves) -- one edit
- Ctrl+- deleted the row of any one cell (and VS Code zoomed out) -> only with whole rows selected
- Shift+Space typed a space into the cell -> the whole row (Ctrl+Space: the column)
- typed over a cell, Left / Right moved the caret -> all four arrows write it and move; F2 = the
  caret at the end (not all selected), F2 again toggles Enter / Edit mode; a double click puts the
  caret where it was clicked
- Ctrl+X cleared at once -> moved when pasted (Esc forgets it)
- Ctrl+R opened VS Code's Open Recent; Ctrl+Z while typing undid the FILE's last edit -> the table
  handles them (package.json binds them to ht9045Designer.csvKey in the table only; csvEditing ctx)
- a cell with a line break lost it when edited -> edited as text only
Added: the active cell = where the selection started (Excel); Ctrl+Enter = the value into every
selected cell; Ctrl+D / Ctrl+R fill; Enter / Tab inside a block; Tab..Tab then Enter back to the
first column; Ctrl+H replace (whole cell, in the selection, replace all = one Ctrl+Z); Shift+Enter /
Shift+F3 previous; Ctrl+arrow to the data's edge; Backspace = the cell from empty; an empty row under
the last one (typing there adds a row); the status bar shows the row's first two columns (which axis)
and sum / average / min / max of the numbers selected; a column click starts under the title row.

Tests: 13 real-input checks (DevTools protocol: real keys / clicks) pass; synthetic: cut, paste
block; lib: the four paste cases; smoke: column fill, repeat, cut move -- one edit each, the
csvEditing context. run_all 3/3 layers (lib 168, smoke 197). The real VS Code layer not run
(VS Code's own update still pending).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
